          "id": "a5L9zwEbTQnPprg5",
          "name": "Rusting Death",
          "kind": "passive",
          "description": "When Theiltemar is destroyed, his bones explode as the necromantic energy holding him together is released. This shreds his rusted chain mail as well, flinging rusty shards of jagged metal in all directions. Adjacent creatures take 2d6 piercing damage (check (reflex, dc:21, basic) save) and are exposed to rust creep. As his remains settled to the floor, the wall of force blocking area F14 flickers and fades.",
