    "data": {
      "schemaVersion": 1,
      "entryType": "HAZARD",
      "name": "Overloading Arch (1-2)",
      "level": 3,
      "rarity": "common",
      "size": "medium",
      "traits": [
        "electricity",
        "magical",
        "trap"
      ],
      "description": "The Eternity Arch sparks with electricity, releasing bolts of lightning at each of the four largest time rifts.",
      "armorClass": 10,
      "hitPoints": 10,
      "hardness": 0,
      "stealth": {
        "modifier": 0,
        "details": ""
      },
      "disable": "check (thievery, dc:20) (trained) or check (arcana, dc:18), check (nature, dc:18), check (occultism, dc:18), or check (religion, dc:18) (trained) to seal each of the four time rifts, check (crafting, dc:20) (trained) to divert the lightning to another source, or Dispel Magic (1st rank; counteract DC 17) to counteract each time rift. Each attempt requires 2 actions. Skill checks to disable a time rift must attempted from adjacent to the rift.",
      "isComplex": true,
      "routine": "(4 actions) The trap loses 1 action each turn for each disabled time rift. On each of the trap's actions, the Eternity Arch releases a bolt of lightning that activates that rift, dealing 2d6 electricity damage to all creatures in a 10-foot emanation around the time rift (check (reflex, dc:20, basic) save). It can release a bolt at each active time rift no more than once each turn.",
      "reset": "",
      "saves": {
        "fortitude": 0,
        "reflex": 0,
        "will": 0
      },
      "defenses": {
        "immunities": [],
        "resistances": [],
        "weaknesses": []
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "5flQveIApZpVwbdw",
          "name": "Shock",
          "kind": "passive",
          "description": "Trigger A creature approaches within 10 feet of one of the time rifts\nEffect The triggering creature takes 1d6 electricity damage (check (reflex, dc:20, basic) save). The overloading arch rolls initiative.",
          "traits": []
        }
      ]
    }
